### Kerberos core questions

Q.1. What is Kerberos, what problem does it solve, and what are its core components?

A: Kerberos is a network authentication protocol that gives steady authentication between a client and a server using encryption and hashes. 
It solves the problem of authentication over an insecure network by implementing its own secure authentication. 
Kerberos includes the Key Distribution Center (KDC) that has the Authentication Server (AS) and the Ticket Granting Service (TGS). 
The client authentication itself is done to the AS infrequently, when logging in or when the ticket granting ticket expires.
When the client needs to communicate with a server it does not have an active ticket with, it goes through communication with the TGS.


